+# Research
+
+## Request paths and current behavior
+
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/api/v1/product/ProductApi.java` maps `DELETE /api/v1/private/product/{id}` to `ProductCommonFacadeImpl.deleteProduct`, which delegates to `ProductServiceImpl.delete`. The product is physically deleted, so future SKU lookups fail. The product delete path itself does not currently clean or rewrite carts/orders.
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/api/v2/product/ProductApiV2.java` maps `GET /api/v2/product/{sku}` to `ProductFacadeV2Impl.getProductByCode`. That facade calls `ProductService.getBySku`; a missing product is converted to `ResourceNotFoundException`, so this endpoint already has the required 404 behavior once deletion remains a normal physical delete.
+- `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/services/catalog/product/ProductServiceImpl.java` implements SKU lookup by querying the product repository. A missing SKU currently becomes a `ServiceException`, rather than a null result.
+
+## Cart failure cause
+
+- `sm-core-model/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/model/shoppingcart/ShoppingCartItem.java` persists the SKU and legacy product id, while its live `Product` reference is transient. This is sufficient to identify a deleted line without retaining a deleted product entity.
+- `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/services/shoppingcart/ShoppingCartServiceImpl.java` reloads carts in `getByCode`/`getById` through `getPopulatedShoppingCart`. `getPopulatedItem` looks up every line by SKU. A deleted SKU currently throws before the existing `product == null` obsolete handling can run.
+- Existing obsolete handling sets `ShoppingCart.obsolete`; `getByCode` and `getById` then call `delete(shoppingCart)` and return null. This breaks the cart endpoint and would also prevent further updates or checkout. An empty cart is likewise treated as obsolete.
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/populator/shoppingCart/ShoppingCartDataPopulator.java` dereferences `item.getProduct()` for SKU/name/price/image, so deleted lines must be removed from the model before this conversion. The calculation service will then calculate totals and quantity from the remaining lines; an empty line-item set naturally produces zero totals.
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/controller/shoppingCart/facade/ShoppingCartFacadeImpl.java` creates new cart lines by SKU and throws `ResourceNotFoundException` when the product is absent. This is the correct 404 behavior for adding a deleted SKU, but the service lookup exception needs to be translated/handled consistently.
+- Checkout code in `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/controller/order/facade/OrderFacadeImpl.java` validates each cart line by SKU. Once deleted lines are filtered during cart reload, checkout sees only live products. A defensive missing-product path is also needed so checkout cannot order or charge a stale line if one reaches it directly.
+
+## Order failure cause
+
+- `sm-core-model/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/model/order/orderproduct/OrderProduct.java` stores `PRODUCT_SKU`, `PRODUCT_NAME`, `PRODUCT_QUANTITY`, and `ONETIME_CHARGE` as independent order-history fields; it has no live product relationship. These fields are the required immutable snapshot, and order totals are based on them.
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/mapper/order/ReadableOrderProductMapper.java` correctly maps SKU, name, quantity, price, and subtotal from `OrderProduct`, but then tries to reload the live product by SKU. When the SKU is gone, `ProductService` throws and the mapper currently wraps/rethrows it, breaking private and customer order reads. The live product enrichment is optional and should be skipped when the lookup fails.
+- The deprecated `ReadableOrderProductPopulator` has the same optional-live-product lookup pattern and should tolerate a missing product as well, to protect any v1/legacy order read path still using it.
+- Order creation is performed by `OrderProductPopulator`, which copies SKU/name/price/quantity from the cart line into `OrderProduct`; preserving these fields makes post-delete order responses and totals independent of the product row.
+
+## Scope and affected behavior
+
+The implementation must therefore (1) remove only missing-product lines while hydrating a cart, (2) preserve and return the cart even when no lines remain, (3) let add-to-cart reject a missing SKU with 404, (4) make checkout ignore/reject stale missing lines without creating an order product, and (5) let order mappers serve the stored snapshot while omitting only optional live-product details. No other product's row or cart/order snapshot should be modified.
+
